Keep Autopilot running until the root agent explicitly completes the task

When an Autopilot turn becomes idle without a successful root-level
`task_complete` call, send a hidden continuation prompt and keep the existing
protocol turn open. Failed calls and subagent completion signals do not finish
the root turn. Share the continuation prompt between local chat and the Agent
Host, and exclude the synthetic message from user persistence and telemetry.

